  "summary": "Reverse shell to ngrok tunnel executed at install time",
  "details": "package.json declares scripts.postinstall = 'node poc.js', which runs automatically on npm install. poc.js opens a TCP connection to 0.tcp.in.ngrok.io:19775, spawns /bin/sh, and pipes the socket into the shell's stdin/stdout, granting the remote party interactive command execution on the installer's host. There is no authentication on the channel and no disclosure of remote-access behavior in the package.",
